        "collapsible_tab_UWQ8gk": {
          "type": "collapsible-tab",
          "name": "Overview",
          "settings": {
            "collapsible_tab_heading": "Overview",
            "collapsible_tab_text": "<h3>Built for the Yard That Fights Back</h3><p>Slopes, tall grass, uneven ground, and leaves — the <strong>Mowrator S1 21\" 2WD</strong> is built to take them on.</p><p>Remote controlled and powered for demanding yard work, it handles slopes up to <strong>45% (24°)</strong> while you stay in control from a comfortable distance.</p><p>The <strong>21\" cutting deck</strong>, rugged traction, and adjustable cutting height give you the control to tackle everything from routine mowing to tougher terrain.</p><p>And when mowing is done, the S1 keeps working. <strong>Mow, mulch, discharge, bag, or vacuum leaves</strong> with its integrated leaf-collection capability.</p><p>Available with <strong>12Ah or 18Ah battery options</strong>, so you can choose the setup that fits your yard and workload.</p><p><strong>One machine. More control. Less work.</strong></p>"
          }
        },
        "collapsible_tab_Uf69Wz": {
          "type": "collapsible-tab",
          "name": "Product Information",
          "settings": {
            "collapsible_tab_heading": "Product Information",
            "collapsible_tab_text": "<h2>Battery & Performance</h2><p>The S1 2WD is available with either a 12Ah or 18Ah battery. Same mower, different runtime for different property sizes.</p><p><strong>12Ah</strong><br/>Up to 1.5 hours runtime and coverage of up to 0.75 acre per charge. Best suited for smaller residential properties.</p><p><strong>18Ah</strong><br/>Up to 2.25 hours runtime and coverage of up to 1.125 acres per charge. Ideal for larger properties or longer mowing sessions.</p><p>Both batteries use a 56V automotive grade LiFePO4 platform, rated for roughly 1,500 charge cycles and capable of fully recharging in about 90 minutes with the included charger.</p><h2>Cutting Power</h2><p>The 21\" steel cutting deck uses a blade motor peaking at 1,985.6W, reaching up to 3,200 RPM with remote adjustable speed and delivering up to 6 ft lb of cutting torque.</p><p>Cutting height adjusts from 1.8\" to 4.6\", with options to mulch, rear bag, or side discharge depending on the job.</p><h2>Drive & Handling</h2><p>The 2WD dual motor drivetrain delivers 500W of total drive power, paired with soft compound traction tires and weighted metal hubcaps.</p><p>The S1 can handle slopes up to 45% (24°), reaches speeds of up to 3.4 mph, and is controlled through a handheld remote rather than app based autonomous navigation.</p><h2>Safety</h2><p>A four point ultrasonic sensor array and front bumper provide collision detection, while a tilt sensor automatically cuts blade power if the mower tips.</p><h2>Warranty</h2><p>2 year warranty covering the main machine, remote, and battery.</p>"
          }
        },
        "collapsible_tab_X7L37G": {
          "type": "collapsible-tab",
          "name": "Warranty & Support",
          "settings": {
            "collapsible_tab_heading": "Warranty & Support",
            "collapsible_tab_text": "<p>Every Mowrator S1 2WD is backed by Mowrator's standard 2 year warranty, covering the main machine, the remote control, and the battery, on both the 12Ah and 18Ah configurations.</p><p><strong>What's covered</strong><br/><br/>Manufacturing defects and functional failures under normal residential use. Warranty service is handled through Mowrator's authorized repair network; you'll need proof of purchase (order date, model, and serial number) to file a claim.</p><p><strong>30 Day Money-Back Guarantee</strong><br/><br/>If the S1 doesn't work out for your yard, return it within 30 days of delivery for a refund. Keep the original packaging on hand for the return window, it makes the process faster.</p><p><strong>Reporting an issue</strong><br/><br/>Inspect your mower on delivery. Shipping damage should be reported within 24 hours, and any other concerns within 7 days, to keep your claim eligible.</p><p><strong>Our role</strong><br/><br/>As your dealer, we're your first point of contact. Reach out to us for setup help, order questions, or to get a warranty claim started, and we'll coordinate directly with Mowrator on your behalf so you're not left navigating it alone.</p>"
          }
        },
        "collapsible_tab_HjeTwa": {
          "type": "collapsible-tab",
          "name": "Setup & Installation",
          "settings": {
            "collapsible_tab_heading": "Setup & Installation",
            "collapsible_tab_text": "<p>Getting the S1 2WD running takes about 15 to 20 minutes, most of it charging.</p><p><strong>In the box</strong><br/><br/>Mower body with 21 inch standard blade, battery (12Ah or 18Ah depending on your selection), charger, wheels, grass outlet cover, remote control, tool bag, manual grass bag, mulching insert, and data cable.</p><p><strong>1. Charge the battery</strong><br/><br/>Before first use, fully charge the battery using the included charger. A full charge typically takes around 90 minutes, though the first charge can run a bit longer.</p><p><strong>2. Assemble the grass bag</strong><br/><br/>Check the bag for damage before installing. Slide the fabric onto the metal frame, then fasten the rubber strips around the bag opening to the frame.</p><p><strong>3. Choose your clipping mode</strong><br/><br/>For mulching, open the grass outlet cover and insert the mulching insert. For bagging, attach the assembled grass bag. For discharge, no attachment is needed.</p><p><strong>4. Seat the battery</strong><br/><br/>Unlock the battery buckle, insert the battery into its compartment until secure, and close the buckle.</p><p><strong>5. Pair the remote</strong><br/><br/>Power on the mower. The remote connects to it wirelessly. Indicator lights confirm connection status.</p><p><strong>6. Set your cutting height</strong><br/><br/>Adjust the deck to your starting height within the 1.8 to 4.6 inch range.</p><p><strong>7. Clear the area and do a test pass</strong><br/><br/>Walk the yard first and remove sticks, toys, hoses, or debris. Keep people and pets clear of the mowing area.</p>"
          }
        },
        "collapsible_tab_czbJiW": {
          "type": "collapsible-tab",
          "name": "Specifications",
          "settings": {
            "collapsible_tab_heading": "Specifications",
            "collapsible_tab_text": "<p>Model: Mowrator S1 21\" 2WD<br/><br/>Drive: Two wheel drive, dual rear motors, 500W total<br/><br/>Cutting width: 21 in<br/><br/>Cutting height range: 1.8 to 4.6 in, adjustable<br/><br/>Blade motor: 1985.6W peak, up to 3200 RPM<br/><br/>Max slope rating: 45% (24°)<br/><br/>Max speed: 3.4 mph<br/><br/>Battery: 56V LiFePO4, available in 12Ah or 18Ah<br/><br/>Runtime: up to 1.5 hours (12Ah) or up to 2.25 hours (18Ah)<br/><br/>Coverage per charge: up to 0.75 acre (12Ah) or up to 1.125 acres (18Ah)<br/><br/>Charge time: approximately 90 minutes<br/><br/>Clipping system: mulch, rear bag, or side discharge<br/><br/>Safety sensors: four point ultrasonic collision detection, front bumper, tilt sensor with automatic blade cutoff<br/><br/>Control method: handheld remote control<br/><br/>Warranty: 2 years on main machine, remote control, and battery<br/><br/></p>"
          }
        },
